  The continuous-time coefficients leave a residual. Diagnose it before blaming
  the derivation: the scale-free orthogonality residual is
    ||J^T D|| / (||J||_F ||D||) = 4.771e-03
  so the ten conditions ARE satisfied to that relative accuracy. rho* is larger
  because it involves (J^T J)^-1, which amplifies whatever is left along the
  weakly excited parameter directions (cond(J) is about 8e+02). The formula is
  right; its COEFFICIENTS need the discrete Jacobian, not its continuous limit.

============================================================================================
7  THE SAME FORMULA, COEFFICIENTS FROM THE PRODUCTION DISCRETE JACOBIAN
============================================================================================
  Identical linear system, 10 x 18 in (M_a, C_a, K_a). Only the coefficients change:
  each is <J_j, Delta_u> for the unit addition u, evaluated through the same block
  and the same `evaluate_step_rows` the basis is built with. This removes the O(Ts)
  gap between the continuous condition and the one-step map that training sees.

  lossless subsystem rank 10 of 12, admissible dimension 2

  M_a =
[[-0.0012  0.0003 -0.0022]
 [ 0.0003  0.     -0.0003]
 [-0.0022 -0.0003  0.0028]]
  K_a =
[[-0.9899  0.0497  0.0404]
 [ 0.0497 -0.0809  0.0032]
 [ 0.0404  0.0032 -0.0971]]

